Port of _patches/typescript/011-ls-codeactions.patch (tsc/internal/ls/codeactions.go) to tsrs.

- CodeAction.Kind: `tsrs_ls::CodeAction::kind` (an `lsproto::CodeActionKind`; empty is Go's ""). The three built-in
  fix providers build their `CodeAction`s with `..Default::default()` for it (Go's zero value).
- externalCodeFixProviders, RegisterCodeFixProvider: `tsrs_ls::register_code_fix_provider(&'static CodeFixProvider)`
  (a process-wide `RwLock<Vec<..>>`); ProvideCodeActions checks the built-in providers, then the external ones.
- RefactorProvider, externalRefactorProviders, RegisterRefactorProvider: `tsrs_ls::{RefactorProvider,
  register_refactor_provider}`; `get_refactor_actions` is a `fn` with Go's parameters (`&'static Program`,
  `&LanguageService`).
- ProvideCodeActions runs the refactor providers after the quick fixes when shouldRunRefactors holds;
  shouldRunRefactors and convertRefactorToLSPCodeAction are ported as is. tsrs's `CodeActionParams::context` is
  not optional, so Go's `params.Context == nil` check is the `only == None` one.

